---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const d='/equipment/06-10/',ref='https://www.newenglandlab.com/userfiles/files/resources/Catalog%20Sections/NEL/NEL_Cambridge%20Tables_Catalog_6_22_20.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Custom dry-table layout and independent projection exercise" description="Orbit an original dry bench concept and examine how a detached rectangular footprint changes with orientation." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment" id="drytable"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/06-10/">← Equipment 06-10</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#dry-evidence">References and checks</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">06-10 / ORIGINAL DRY FURNITURE · DETACHED GEOMETRY</p><h2>Turn a footprint without changing its size</h2><p class="eq-lede">Inspect an original bench concept with an empty top and fixed storage outline. On the separate stand, turn a fictional rectangle and check its projected dimensions against a frame.</p></header>
<div class="dry-cols"><section><h3>Concept furniture</h3><canvas id="dry-model" aria-label="Orbitable dry bench and physically separate footprint stand"></canvas><p id="dry-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="dry-front">Reset overview</button><button id="dry-furniture">Furniture closer</button><button id="dry-board">Detached puzzle</button></section>
<section><h3>Detached plan-view check</h3>
<svg id="dry-chart" viewBox="0 0 180 145" role="img" aria-label="Fictional reference frame, rotating rectangle and its dashed bounding box"><rect width="180" height="145" fill="#20343a"/><rect x="26" y="17.5" width="128" height="110" fill="none" stroke="#80d1bd" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect id="dry-token" x="30" y="47.5" width="120" height="50" fill="#d4a64f" fill-opacity=".68" stroke="#ffd48b"/><rect id="dry-projected" x="30" y="47.5" width="120" height="50" fill="none" stroke="#fff1d0" stroke-dasharray="3 2"/></svg>
<label>Orientation <select id="dry-pose"><option value="aligned">0° · aligned</option><option value="diagonal">36.87° · diagonal</option><option value="right">90° · right angle</option></select></label><button id="dry-next">Next orientation</button>
<p id="dry-readout" role="status"></p><p>Total horizontal / vertical margin: <strong id="dry-clearance"></strong>. A negative total margin indicates overhang, not clearance on either side. This doesn't predict collisions while turning.</p>
<button id="dry-export">Download geometry result</button><p><a href={d+'example-footprint.json'}>Example diagonal check</a>.</p></section></div>
<section id="dry-evidence"><h3>Design basis and references</h3><div class="dry-cols"><figure><img src={d+'station.webp'} alt="Original empty dry table concept, drawers and an unrelated teaching stand"/><figcaption>Original furniture, not an installed instrument. <a href={ref+'#page=6'}>New England Lab Cambridge furniture catalogue, TWA base table photo and 60 × 30 in comparator</a> is a styling comparator for straight legs, frame and rectangular top only. The dimensions and storage assembly are original design choices.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={d+'board.webp'} alt="Separate dark footprint plan board with its gold tile turned diagonally"/><figcaption>Detached plan-view stand. The board is not a work area or accessory of the table. One pose chosen at a time, without movement or collision constraints.</figcaption></figure></div>
<table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Known expected result</th><th>Verified result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nominal furniture W × H × D</td><td>1,524 × 914.4 × 762 mm</td><td>Design dimensions, not survey; GLB within 0.5 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Align 120 × 50 tile</td><td>+8 / +60 total margin</td><td>Exact · fits</td></tr><tr><td>Diagonal 3–4–5 orientation</td><td>126 × 112 footprint; +2 / −2 margin</td><td>Exact · does not fit</td></tr><tr><td>Right angle 90°</td><td>50 × 120 footprint</td><td>Exact · does not fit</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>The footprint is the axis-aligned bounding rectangle of the rotated tile: its width and height use the absolute sine and cosine projections. No material, power, casting, curing, setup, geometry transfer, or process apparatus is modeled. The register's original process acceptance is unsupported.</p><p><a href={d+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={d+'dry-table.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={d+'plan-view.mjs'}>Detached action and report code</a> · <a href={d+'vr.json'}>VR target and travel</a>. Headset use not verified.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/06-10/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>
#drytable .dry-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.15fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#drytable section{margin:1rem 0;padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);min-width:0}
#drytable :is(button,select){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.4rem;margin:.2rem .25rem .2rem 0;max-width:100%}#drytable button{cursor:pointer}#drytable :is(button,select):focus-visible{outline:2px solid #b28d5e}
#dry-model{width:100%;height:354px;display:block;touch-action:none}#dry-chart{display:block;width:min(100%,320px);margin:.4rem auto}#drytable figure{margin:.5rem 0}#drytable figure img{width:100%}
#drytable table{width:100%;font-size:.94rem;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left}#drytable td,#drytable th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}
@media(max-width:850px){#drytable .dry-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#dry-model{height:282px}}
</style>
